15246342401001-62570adf-47f9-434b-87a6-5bebd9fbcf21"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"031678a7929c0c74939e0e9b5182fae38abf6fa7ab6cd91df346690698e62c00","event_uuid":"2395f4c8-1c81-4cdf-8ff7-22947898e387","position":{"commit_sha":"025f7485a97f4c98897e7c4b9edcf2cc41ab9b93","position":"1785915453370742001-2395f4c8-1c81-4cdf-8ff7-22947898e387"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"45d0d1bf18274a0c217efd76fcb4f8e40037cf6f729d485dadeb2ffce9a0bd5f","event_uuid":"e917acbe-46e6-4018-b666-b44307ee784f","position":{"commit_sha":"36c89e0420f54777ef246a97b6c7c775384baeff","position":"1785915565387755001-e917acbe-46e6-4018-b666-b44307ee784f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"963502e465c9679aafef57e60c0d2831492341be799fba4ee82aaf07181e7f1f","event_uuid":"f356d505-c328-4972-b4b9-40a91ef1ac33","position":{"commit_sha":"36c89e0420f54777ef246a97b6c7c775384baeff","position":"1785915566126952001-f356d505-c328-4972-b4b9-40a91ef1ac33"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785891885207095001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2403ad44-2927-43c3-bfee-a2f1d4afaf35","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"531b-a5a7-91a2-4e4c"},{"link_uuid":"06cea3c3-91a5-4d4a-97a8-245813c643d1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0fa4-a836-5f13-4a44"},{"link_uuid":"70ec06fe-e063-4341-9b64-c83bf7a710ad","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a40f-25e4-885c-4cca"},{"link_uuid":"e39e1650-411f-4b94-b29c-4368ce6f844a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2801-41d0-c6c0-4ba1"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`_REBAR_OVERRIDES` (src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:282) family-forces\n`native_structured_output: False` for Claude — a blanket signed-contract posture. E1 (recorded\non the selection bug ticket df3a, \"EXPERIMENT RESULTS\" comment: 39 live Bedrock calls, account\n896586841071 / us-east-1) measured native structured output working under extended thinking on\nspecific Bedrock cells. The established mechanism for per-cell measured facts already exists:\n`_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` (capabilities.py:317), an exact-id table that wins over the\nfamily default. Enable exactly the measured cells; every other cell stays fail-closed.\n\nBedrock capability facts are account/region-scoped — this same epic saw a Bedrock fact\nfalsified on re-measurement in the project account — so each enabling row records the E1\naccount/region it was measured in and a re-measure trigger, and the enablement is scoped to the\nexact measured ids only.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` rows setting `native_structured_output: True` and\n`native_output_with_thinking: True` for the cells E1 measured PASS:\n`us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` (adaptive thinking) and\n`us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` (the dated profile id — the bare haiku alias 400s\nat request validation; measured E1).\n\n**Plumb `native_output_with_thinking` through EVERY `ModelCapabilities(...)` construction site\nthat feeds `output_mode` (currently inert — this is the load-bearing part of this story, not just\nthe rows).** `output_mode` (src/rebar/llm/structured.py:46) already reads\n`caps.native_output_with_thinking`, and the field exists on `ModelCapabilities` (introduced by\nthe guard story 0fa4, fail-closed default False), BUT a `ModelCapabilities(` sweep shows THREE\nlive construction sites, and ALL THREE omit the field so it defaults False:\n\n1. `_capabilities_from_profile` (capabilities.py ~:341) — omits it from both its `caps` seed\n   dict and its constructor call.\n2. The string-fallback path (capabilities.py ~:474-486) — omits it from its `merged` seed dict\n   and its constructor call.\n3. `_intersect_capabilities` (src/rebar/llm/runner.py:696) — the CONSERVATIVE record for a\n   `FallbackModel` chain, fed DIRECTLY into `output_mode`; it intersects every other field with\n   `all(...)` across candidates but has no `native_output_with_thinking` line, so a chain of the\n   measured cells collapses the field to False and routes PromptedOutput under thinking.\n\n(A `ModelCapabilities(` sweep also finds a fourth occurrence — the module constant\n`_CONSERVATIVE` at capabilities.py:429 — but that is the intended fail-closed record and must\nSTAY `native_output_with_thinking=False`; the string-fallback seed reads it, so it is set\nexplicitly to False there for clarity, not plumbed from an override.)\n\nSo an override that sets `native_output_with_thinking: True` is silently DROPPED on all three\noverride-carrying paths. This story fixes all three: seed the field in the two capabilities.py dicts (profile path:\ndefault False; fallback path: from `_CONSERVATIVE.native_output_with_thinking`) and pass\n`native_output_with_thinking=bool(...)` in both those constructor calls; and add\n`native_output_with_thinking=all(c.native_output_with_thinking for c in per_candidate)` to\n`_intersect_capabilities` (the conservative `all` intersection, identical to every sibling field\nthere — a chain claims native-under-thinking only when EVERY candidate is measured to support\nit). This plumbing is exactly what 0fa4 deferred by leaving the default fail-closed \"until the\nrows story records measured PASS cells\" — it is inseparable from the rows and belongs to this\nstory.\n\nEach row's comment cites its measuring run: E1 (df3a \"EXPERIMENT RESULTS\" — outputConfig\njson_schema + thinking proven wire-legal, no 400: sonnet-4-6 adaptive, haiku-4-5 budget 2048;\naccount 896586841071 / us-east-1). Client-side Pydantic validators remain mandatory on the\nnative path — Bedrock's schema transform strips `ge`/`le` bounds (measured E1: emitted 1.0\nout-of-bounds).\n\nExplicit non-rows, recorded in the table comment: Bedrock opus-4-7/4-8 are rejected server-side\nby Converse structured output under thinking (provider rollout gap; re-measure trigger: rerun\nthe harness cell when AWS announces support). NOTE these two ids ALREADY carry a\n`supports_temperature: False` row (ticket 2932/1903) — this story adds NO\nnative-structured-output / native-under-thinking row for them, so they remain fail-closed to\nPromptedOutput; they are \"non-rows\" only with respect to the native-output capability.\nDirect-Anthropic and OpenAI cells gain rows only from a harness matrix run measured PASS\n(operator-attested artifact); cells without credentials at run time are recorded \"unmeasured\"\nand stay prompted.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py — the measured-cell rows, the `native_output_with_thinking`\n  plumbing through the two `ModelCapabilities(...)` construction sites here (profile +\n  string-fallback), and the non-row comment\n- src/rebar/llm/runner.py — the third construction site: `native_output_with_thinking` added to\n  `_intersect_capabilities`'s `all(...)` intersection (FallbackModel chains)\n- tests/unit/ (capabilities test file) — config-effect contrast tests, including a pin that the\n  override actually reaches the constructed record\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier, config-effect contrast through the real capability read path (resolve model id ->\ncapabilities -> `output_mode`):\n\n- `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` with thinking=True -> NativeOutput.\n- The dated haiku id (`us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`) with thinking=True ->\n  NativeOutput.\n- Plumbing pin (regression pin for the review BLOCK): the constructed `ModelCapabilities` for a\n  measured cell has `native_output_with_thinking is True` — a mutation dropping the field from\n  ANY of the three constructor calls turns this RED (proves the override is not inert).\n- FallbackModel-chain pin: a `_intersect_capabilities` over candidates that ALL support\n  native-under-thinking yields `native_output_with_thinking True` (and a chain mixing a\n  measured cell with a non-measured one yields False — the conservative `all`) -> output_mode\n  routes NativeOutput / PromptedOutput accordingly. A mutation dropping the field from\n  `_intersect_capabilities` turns the all-supporting case RED.\n- String-fallback coverage: `\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\"` passed as a STRING (not\n  an object) also resolves to native_output_with_thinking True -> NativeOutput under thinking,\n  so both construction paths are covered.\n- `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` (carries only the `supports_temperature: False` row, no\n  native/thinking row) with thinking=True -> PromptedOutput (fail-closed negative control).\n- An arbitrary unknown Claude id -> PromptedOutput (family default preserved).\n\nAll deterministic — no live boundary in this story (the live measurement is the harness story's\noperator-attested artifact, already recorded; this story only encodes its result).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both measured Bedrock cells return NativeOutput under thinking through the real read path,\n      on BOTH the object and string-fallback construction paths — checked by the new contrast\n      unit tests.\n- [ ] Opus (temperature-row-only) and unknown-id Claude cells stay PromptedOutput under\n      thinking — checked by the same tests.\n- [ ] `native_output_with_thinking: True` set in an override row reaches the constructed\n      `ModelCapabilities` (the plumbing is not inert) — checked by a dedicated pin that goes RED\n      if ANY of the three construction sites (profile, string-fallback, `_intersect_capabilities`)\n      omits the field.\n- [ ] A `FallbackModel` chain whose candidates ALL support native-under-thinking preserves\n      `native_output_with_thinking True` (and a mixed chain collapses to False) — checked by the\n      `_intersect_capabilities` contrast test.\n- [ ] Every enabling row's comment cites its measurement evidence (E1 account/region + the\n      wire-legal finding) and the non-row comment records the opus/4-7 re-measure trigger —\n      checked in code review.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Any non-Bedrock row added under this ticket links its harness matrix\n      artifact as a comment here; if none ran (this story adds only the two measured Bedrock\n      rows), the non-Bedrock cells are recorded \"unmeasured\" in the table comment instead.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","reason":"measured-cell rows + opus non-row comment"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_capabilities.py","reason":"config-effect contrast through real read path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0fa4-a836-5f13-4a44"],["depends_on","531b-a5a7-91a2-4e4c"],["depends_on","a40f-25e4-885c-4cca"],["parent","196d-28c4-ef0f-445c"],["relates_to","2801-41d0-c6c0-4ba1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"196d-28c4-ef0f-445c","parent_status_uuid":"e917acbe-46e6-4018-b666-b44307ee784f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"18ae-27e9-b651-4b71","ticket_type":"story","title":"Enable native structured output for measured Bedrock model cells","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d9d0d986-302c-4375-ace2-b5530361c2f2","2403ad44-2927-43c3-bfee-a2f1d4afaf35","06cea3c3-91a5-4d4a-97a8-245813c643d1","70ec06fe-e063-4341-9b64-c83bf7a710ad","20278c38-c42b-4dbf-88ad-b2369a459cca","eebcfffd-1aff-47ca-abc6-a200a0b9d8c2","b83e9308-70ba-4ba9-9798-c374af2f7db6","62570adf-47f9-434b-87a6-5bebd9fbcf21","2395f4c8-1c81-4cdf-8ff7-22947898e387","e917acbe-46e6-4018-b666-b44307ee784f","f356d505-c328-4972-b4b9-40a91ef1ac33","e39e1650-411f-4b94-b29c-4368ce6f844a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785918738719664965,"uuid":"fd73b0de-933b-4512-816f-dcf66787953b"}